################################################################################
# This .gitignore file was automatically created by Microsoft(R) Visual Studio.
################################################################################

/.vs
/_site/
/.idea/
/node_modules/

# Editor workspace config — machine-specific (absolute paths, personal settings).
/.vscode/

# ── Documents ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This is a public repository. Internal working documents committed here are
# world-readable, so no .md is tracked by default — the strategy plan that used
# to live in .docs/ now sits outside the repo entirely.
#
# The four exceptions below are NOT documentation; they are part of the build
# and removing them breaks the site:
#   legals/*.md  -> rendered into /privacy.html and /terms.html via include_relative
#   _posts/*.md  -> the blog itself
#   CLAUDE.md    -> the conventions Claude Code reads before touching this repo
*.md
!legals/*.md
!_posts/*.md
!CLAUDE.md

# Local tooling: useful on a developer's machine, no reason to publish.
.claude/
.docs/
